  "decision_rule": "A family is not eligible for implementation acceptance unless every metric meets its fixed threshold on frozen holdout data, all evidence references validate, budget overruns and unauthorized capabilities are zero, the signed sovereignty attestation is compatible, and independent review closes all critical and high findings.",
  "observations": [
    "The existing synthetic corpus supplies contract and adversarial fixtures but is too small to estimate production prevalence.",
    "Remote analyzers cannot be labeled deterministic from repeated observations."
  ],
  "inferences": [
    "Separate calibration and holdout splits reduce optimistic confidence estimates.",
    "Family-specific metrics are necessary because one aggregate score would hide evidence, abstention, cost, and sovereignty failures."
  ],
  "uncertainties": [
    "Final production datasets and labels require later privacy-approved collection.",
    "External provider revisions and hidden serving changes remain opaque."
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Which constrained extension transport will replace the rejected plain subprocess boundary?",
    "What minimum production sample size supports per-harm calibration and subgroup analysis?"
  ],
